On Sun, Oct 26, 2014 at 9:02 PM, <sunrise2000@comcast.net> wrote:
>
>
> All three of these "lujvo" pass the tosmabru test as laid out on p. 71.
> {cc} is not a valid initial consonant pair, so the test passes and
> doesn't demand a tosmabru y-hyphen.


You're quite right, this is a known erratum in the printed version:
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/CLL,+aka+Reference+Grammar,+Errata

You can find the correct version of rule 5a) in
http://lojban.github.io/cll/4/11/

At this point, I'm so confused I'm not even sure what the proper form
> for a lujvo is.  Does anyone have a formal description (i.e., grammar
> rules) for what constitutes a valid lujvo?


The PEG morphology gives formal grammar rules for all word forms:

 http://www.lojban.org/tiki/BPFK+Section%3A+PEG+Morphology+Algorithm

mu'o mi'e xorxes

